scope: |
  Sergiy's decision 2026-07-28, taken with the corrected premise on the table: the CI argument for
  this is GONE (after `ci-bookkeeping-floods-verdicts`, ZERO bookkeeping commits create a CI run),
  so this is purely about board cadence — 202 of 253 commits in 6 hours carry no code, and the
  20-minute staleness threshold is the forcing function: every live claim must commit at least that
  often, and agents commit more often than that to be safe.

  Change: staleness threshold 20 min -> 45 min, in the two places that state it —
  `scripts/coord-status:387` (1200 -> 2700 seconds, and the `older-than-20m` reason string) and
  `AGENTS.md:1026`. Plus one line of guidance: heartbeat on a MATERIAL status change, not as
  running commentary.

  STATED COST, not hidden: an abandoned claim now blocks its work for up to 45 minutes instead of
  20. That protection has already earned its keep once — the whole board was orphaned with the
  newest heartbeat 21 hours old — so the threshold is being relaxed, not removed, and the triage
  path (`/multi-agent triage <slug>`) is unchanged.

  NOT changing: `.agents/plugins/multi-agent/commands/multi-agent.md` also states "20 minutes", but
  it is a SUBMODULE (separate repo) — if the two disagree, that is scope drift of exactly the kind
  claim-mutex exists to catch. Flagging it in BUGS rather than editing another repo from here.
next: implement, verify coord-status still flags a genuinely stale claim, then return to the queue
